        "# Where You Grow Up Matters: Predicting Adult Income for Low-Income Children in the DC Region\n",
        "## Capstone Two: Pre-processing and Training Data Development\n",
        "\n",
        "**Project question:** Which neighborhood characteristics best predict how much children from low-income families earn as adults, across census tracts in the DC metro area?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal of this notebook:** create a cleaned development dataset that is ready for the modeling step. It starts from `data/processed/eda_features.csv` (saved at the end of the EDA notebook) and works through the three steps in the assignment, in this order:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Create dummy features** for categorical variables\n",
        "2. **Split** the data into training and testing sets\n",
        "3. **Standardize** the numeric features with a scaler\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why this order:** dummies come first because the split and the scaler need numbers; the split comes before scaling so the scaler learns only from the training data (otherwise information from the test set leaks into training).\n",
        "\n",
        "**How to use this notebook**\n",
        "1. In Colab, upload `eda_features.csv` (the last cells of the EDA notebook save it), or run the upload cell in Section 1.\n",
        "2. Run the cells from top to bottom.\n",
        "3. The cells labeled **Write-up note** are drafted in first person with the numbers this notebook produces. Read each one, confirm the numbers match your own output, and rewrite it in your own words.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Rubric check:** every DSM step is completed (dummy features, scale standardization, train/test split); the notes show *when* and *why* each step is applied; a working, commented notebook uploaded in full to GitHub."
      ]
    },
