        "**Write-up note (summary):**\n",
        "I started from the EDA table of 735 tracts. I found one categorical variable (state) and predictors on very different scales, so I (1) created dummy columns for state with DC as the baseline, (2) split the data 80/20 with a fixed random seed, stratified by state, into 588 training and 147 testing tracts, and (3) standardized the 15 continuous predictors using a scaler fit on the training set only. The final predictor table has 17 columns (15 scaled predictors and 2 state dummies). I saved the scaled training and testing sets, the targets, the weights, and the scaler's parameters in `data/processed/`. The next step is modeling, starting from those files.\n",
